  "worked_solution": "The range of $\\sqrt{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts do not affect the range. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x-3}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $\\frac{3}{5}$ and then adding $3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x-3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt{x-3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt{x-3}+3 & \\ge 3 \\\\ f(x) & \\ge 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in [3,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14239347/assets/c27b96134ab2d7004262d14163db2cd3714fd0c18fb6bb84444252d5bdac2ef7.png)",
